\details{
\code{specify_dynam()} reads a formula written for goldfish, for an MRQAP in
\code{{infernet}}, or for \code{{ergm}}, and returns the goldfish model it describes.
Its left-hand side names the dependent layer, as in \code{\link[=estimate_dynam]{estimate_dynam()}}, so
one formula can move between models. It is proposed as the successor of
\code{\link[=make_specification]{make_specification()}}: with \code{.data}, it returns the same \code{goldfishSpec}.
\itemize{
\item A term that goldfish has under another name is rewritten as it, as
ergm's \code{nodematch("dept")} becomes \code{same(dept)}, and infernet's
\code{exchange(friends)} becomes \code{recip(friends)}.
\item A term that goldfish defines differently, such as infernet's \code{sim()}, is
kept and named.
\item A term that goldfish cannot fit is dropped and named, so that the rest
still fits: an ergm term without a goldfish effect, such as \code{gwesp()},
infernet's \code{mix()} or random intercepts, and, with \code{.data}, a main effect
that the sub-model cannot identify, such as \code{ego()} in a choice model.
}

Rewritten and differently read terms are reported with \code{\link[cli:cli_inform]{cli::cli_inform()}},
and dropped terms in one warning. A name that no model knows is left for
\code{\link[=make_specification]{make_specification()}}, which aborts.
}
\section{A table of every effect}{

Without a formula, or with \code{.} as its whole right-hand side, as in
\code{calls ~ .}, \code{specify_dynam()} returns a table of every effect that
goldfish can build for \code{.data} in \code{model} and \code{sub_model}, as
\code{RSiena::getEffects()} does for a Siena data object. Each effect is
written out for the network's layers and node attributes:
\itemize{
\item an effect of a network, such as \code{inertia} or \code{indeg()}, on its own,
where it reads the dependent layer, and with each other layer, and
with \code{type = "ego"} where it has a \code{type};
\item an effect of an attribute, \code{ego()}, \code{alter()}, and \code{same()}, for each
node attribute, and \code{diff()} and \code{sim()} for each numeric one;
\item \code{tertius()} and \code{tertius_diff()} for each layer and numeric attribute;
\item \code{global()} for each global variable.
}

A label, a name, \code{active}, or an attribute with a different category for
every node gets no effect. The closures through two layers, such as
\code{mixed_trans()}, are not listed.
Each row's status is \code{\link[=make_specification]{make_specification()}} of that effect alone:
\code{"fits"}, or \code{"drops"} with goldfish's reason.

The table is a tibble of class \code{"goldfishTerms"}, with the columns \code{term},
\code{effect}, \code{layer}, \code{attribute}, \code{status}, and \code{reason}. Choose rows with
\code{[} or \code{dplyr::filter()}, and \code{formula()} of the rows gives the
specification of those effects.
}

